  "content": {
    "id": "v2-dd963-p17-practice-slot-7-upper-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Solve $\\sqrt2\\sin x\\cos x=\\cos x$ for $x\\in[0,2\\pi)$. Answer in exact form if possible, otherwise round to 3 d.p.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{3\\pi}{4},\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt2\\sin x\\cos x-\\cos x&=0\\\\\\cos x(\\sqrt2\\sin x-1)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $\\cos x=0$ or $\\sin x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}$.\n\nFor $\\cos x=0$, $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$.\n\nFor $\\sin x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt2}$, the reference angle is $A=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$. Sine is positive in Q1 and Q2, so $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{3\\pi}{4}$.\n\nTherefore $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{3\\pi}{4},\\frac{3\\pi}{2}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": null
  },
